WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.227 --> 00:00:02.727
(piano music)

00:00:04.928 --> 00:00:08.845
- [Old Woman] Colma is
a very unique community.

00:00:12.672 --> 00:00:15.331
We have a million and a
half underground residents,

00:00:15.331 --> 00:00:17.498
and 1700 living residents.

00:00:22.461 --> 00:00:25.211
We have become the city of souls.

00:00:27.552 --> 00:00:30.135
(guitar music)

00:00:31.397 --> 00:00:33.122
My name is Pat Hatfield,

00:00:33.122 --> 00:00:37.900
and I am the retired historian
for the town of Colma.

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:41.817
I have lived here now
for 65 years, since 1950.

00:00:43.239 --> 00:00:45.064
We have now 17 cemeteries.

00:00:45.064 --> 00:00:47.762
I call us the United
Nations of cemeteries,

00:00:47.762 --> 00:00:50.530
because we have a cemetery for everyone.

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:52.275
We have, for instance,

00:00:52.275 --> 00:00:54.164
we have four Jewish cemeteries,

00:00:54.164 --> 00:00:55.901
we have a Catholic cemetery,

00:00:55.901 --> 00:00:57.409
a Greek cemetery,

00:00:57.409 --> 00:00:59.076
an Italian cemetery.

00:01:00.418 --> 00:01:03.450
(piano music)

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:06.117
And we even have a pet cemetery.

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:13.498
We have very famous
people like Wyatt Earp,

00:01:13.498 --> 00:01:14.742
and Joe Dimaggio,

00:01:14.742 --> 00:01:16.697
and William Randolph Hearst,

00:01:16.697 --> 00:01:18.364
and it just goes on.

00:01:24.075 --> 00:01:27.334
We inherited hundreds of
thousands of bodies because,

00:01:27.334 --> 00:01:28.692
during the gold rush,

00:01:28.692 --> 00:01:30.742
so many gold miners came here,

00:01:30.742 --> 00:01:32.408
and with them,

00:01:32.408 --> 00:01:34.225
they brought so many diseases

00:01:34.225 --> 00:01:38.548
that San Francisco
innocently had 27 cemeteries.

00:01:38.548 --> 00:01:40.035
And they were full.

00:01:40.035 --> 00:01:41.088
The city father said,

00:01:41.088 --> 00:01:45.255
"Our land is to be for the
living, not for the dead."

00:01:47.379 --> 00:01:51.586
So, an eviction notice was passed in 1914,

00:01:51.586 --> 00:01:55.753
and the bodies were slowly
transferred here to Colma.

00:01:57.417 --> 00:02:00.769
The Colma residents really
respect our cemeteries,

00:02:00.769 --> 00:02:02.754
but we call them our parks.

00:02:02.754 --> 00:02:04.273
That's what they are.

00:02:04.273 --> 00:02:05.106
We picnic them,

00:02:05.106 --> 00:02:06.872
we walk in them,

00:02:06.872 --> 00:02:09.735
our children play in them.

00:02:09.735 --> 00:02:11.902
They're just a part of us.

00:02:14.016 --> 00:02:16.599
We do have a slower pulse here,

00:02:17.916 --> 00:02:18.916
almost dead.

00:02:20.467 --> 00:02:22.967
(piano music)

